<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>qr_pad_v1</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>g0rk</name>
  </author>
  <description>
    A 2 m x 2 m QR-coded ground panel with side plates 3 m tall, angled at
    45 degrees. Per the TEKNOFEST rulebook, p.17.

    HOW IT DIFFERS from qr_pad - the texture was corrected:
      QR Version 1 (21x21 modules). The competition uses Version 1.
      Quiet zone of 2 modules (80 px / 840 px). The base model had 0.2
      modules (8 px / 984 px); the standard asks for 4, and too small a
      quiet zone shortens the decode range.
    The geometry is IDENTICAL to qr_pad; only
    materials/textures/qr_code.png differs.
    This is the model the world actually uses (sim/worlds/qr_target.sdf).
  </description>
</model>